+# Named N25 infrastructure continuation: CPU implementation contract
+
+This source implements only the frozen protocol c0c9fac3. Existing W, history, budget and GPU remain untouched by CPU delivery. No blueprint is an executable authority. Science, RDT, native arithmetic/witness, profiles, provider/Stage/E2/180s, decoder and original N25 classifier remain unchanged. Shared delta is exactly runner.metered_support/check_budget/check_retry and worker.validate_context. run_plan, build_command, run_worker and verify_receipt remain byte-identical.
+
+The new operational cohort is N25_ACTUATOR_CLIPPED_RBF_DEV_INFRA_CONTINUATION_V1_20260930. Import exactly18 original accepted cells as immutable metadata evidence; never dispatch or fabricate ledger events for them. New22 map original indices18..39. Only index18 retries the exact named failed task4/N23, with recovery bucket/retry_of plus n25_named_infrastructure_proof. Remaining5 baseline+16 development cells keep their science/seed/init order. Any new invalidity closes immediately, without old timeout recovery or automatic resume. Original INVALID remains immutable and all19 old costs/unknowns remain.
+
+The combined ceiling stays42 attempts/two recoveries, though observed19 old/no recovery plus22 new implies at most41 with one recovery. Original22 local GPU hours do not reset; old8201.788167113322s are subtracted. Root freezes remaining_local_gpu_hours no greater than min(22-old/3600, actual remaining unprotected cumulative hours). Every dispatch needs1840s. Private494/100 and55/199/180/40/20 caps plus32/12 protected hours are exact, with no amendment here. Cumulative accounting retains the original tensor resource proof and requires its health ledger settlement; there is no new preflight.
+
+## Metadata sealer and reliance
+
+Root runs qd_ed_n25_cont_seal.py only after reviewing this final source, while original5a W still exists. It imports only the new stdlib evidence helper and does not import old contracts or invoke their full validators. Input envelope:
+
+```
+{schema: n25-continuation-sealing-input-v1,
+ root_authorized: true,
+ references: {review, result, source, plan, controller, stage_public},
+ files: [{path: absolute_metadata_file, sha256: exact_bytes}, ...]}
+```
+
+Each reference is exactly path/sha256. The four frozen review/result/source/plan hashes are pinned by protocol; root_authorized cannot substitute for them. The allowlist is at most512 unique resolved files, each at most16MiB and all read bytes at most128MiB. Stat/size checks happen before bounded allocation; changed size/hash, symlinks, unlisted ref or payload suffix fails. Approved formats are JSON/JSONL/text; decision_evidence/images/videos directories and all tensor suffixes are refused. Original source257 are separately read as approved source bytes, never models/weights.
+
+Required manifest closure: old review/result/plan/source/controller/status/Dev-only ledger/runtime JSON;18 accepted cells' terminal/context/receipt/audit plus process/audit-start JSON; failed terminal/process/context and results.txt/episode_compute presence; original source-review/authority/backend proof and four proof refs; public Stage projection. Budget authority/release can be included for root use. Raw Stage file, tensors and runtime.files/model paths are never followed. Reader caches each inventoried metadata payload within one build.
+
+Public Stage projection schema is n25-public-stage-metadata-v1, all43 calls, root attestation and underlying source-stage ref, response_payloads_included=false. It includes no raw_response key, prompts, images or guidance semantics. The root-generated projection is trusted as a hash-bound metadata extraction; source_stage_events and reader references are recorded, not opened. All6 named failed steps, counters, timeout>=180s, cleanup/exit ordering, event/item types and ordered lifecycle association are checked. Null reasoning token counters are preserved. No API-only causal explanation is inferred.
+
+Seal schema n25-continuation-metadata-seal-v1 binds exact18 accepted metadata, all19 old terminals, old source/runtime/plan/authority/proof, recorded evidence index digests, costs and Unknowns. Thousands of receipt evidence.files entries are digested as JSON only; no tensor ref is followed or rehashed. This attests original metered audit plus root terminal review, not a fresh numerical/safety audit. The failed native gates remain UNKNOWN_MISSING, all_non_transport_gates_verified=false, causal attribution UNPROVEN. Literal event=valid/outcome_valid=false/compute_outcome=completed are preserved.
+
+Root must freeze two typed absent audit paths; a late file/symlink fails subsequent history checks. Public /proc boot/PID/start-tick/process-group/session/command checks reject live owned processes/descendants; no signalling occurs. Current proof does not infer unmeasured safety semantics from results/compute presence. Sealer does not consult actual success to choose a prefix: exact18 and0/5,0/5,0/4,1/4 are preregistered original metadata.
+
+## Root records and paths
+
+Control directory is N25/infrastructure-continuation-v1, separate from native artifact_root/attempts. Existing original paths are never overwritten. Files to create only after root review:
+
+- metadata-seal-v1.json, then root-seal-review-v1.json: exact schema n25-continuation-root-seal-review-v1, accepted=true, seal/protocol refs, original_disposition=INVALID_OR_INTERRUPTED, history_is_metadata_attestation=true, historical_unknowns equal frozen constants, gpu_authorized=false.
+- source-bridge-v1.json: bridge.build(new full source, sealed history, owning W);255 old files byte-identical, exactly two whole-file reverse patches/four functions, additional files closed. Historical proof remains labeled old5a; no new arithmetic claim.
+- final-source-runtime-review-v1.json: schema n25-continuation-source-runtime-review-v1, accepted=true, exact source/runtime/protocol/seal/root_seal_review/source_bridge/historical_backend_proof refs, no_new_preflight=true, gpu_authorized=false.
+- adoption-v1/authority.json: schema n25-continuation-authority-v1; cohort_id; exact source/runtime/protocol/seal/final_review/existing_budget_authority; caps and limits; original_local_gpu_hours22; old_gpu_seconds8201.788167113322; finite remaining_local_gpu_hours; nonempty recorded_at/authority_interpretation; validation_authorized=false/formal_authorized=false. Root privately binds n25_continuation_authority to its hash; existing n25_budget_authority/caps stay unchanged.
+- plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json: copied original plan except reviewed source/code_files/new22 rows, new cohort metadata, original-plan derived_from and n25_cohort audit-family marker. Candidate/profile/runtime/seed/input paths remain exact. New plan freeze is immutable.
+- execution-release-v1.json: schema n25-continuation-execution-release-v1; plan/source_commit/cohort_id/authority/seal/ordered22episode_keys/limits/physical_gpu7/one_launch=true; validation/formal false.
+
+Supervisor writes execution/controller-process-v1.json with schema n25-continuation-controller-process-v1, process{pid,proc_start_ticks,boot_id}, plan/release refs and source_commit while holding supervisor ownership. This is not a release. It writes execution/supervisor-status-v1.json and finally result-v1.json plus immutable terminal-ledger-v1.json. Reservation or existing controller result/status blocks another launch. All original/continuation costs are separate and combined by unique attempt_id; unknown token calls are counted or explicitly unmeasured, never filled with zero.
+
+## Exact root activation order
+
+1. Review final CPU logs/source/route bridge and the root-generated metadata inventory. Create a NEW authorized sealing input; never flip/overwrite a previously frozen disabled draft. Under old5a: `PYTHON I/scripts/qd_ed_n25_cont_seal.py --input AUTHORIZED_INPUT --old-root W --output N25/infrastructure-continuation-v1/metadata-seal-v1.json`. Root inspects metadata-only seal and writes root-seal-review. No actual proof or history read was done by executor.
+2. Integrate exact reviewed continuation commit into idle owning W only after original source sealing. Build full source record from bridge.source_paths/worker.source_record; build source bridge; root rechecks runtime/resource/budget/proof settlement and seals final review plus finite authority/private state binding. Source paths/module ownership must resolve to W, never an adjacent clone.
+3. `PYTHON W/scripts/qd_ed_n25_cont_prepare.py --freeze --output N25/infrastructure-continuation-v1/plan.frozen.v1.gpu7.json`. Root inspects22 commands and exact current Codex managed-login settings, then writes explicit execution release.
+4. `PYTHON W/scripts/qd_ed_n25_cont_supervise.py --plan PLAN --release RELEASE --status N25/infrastructure-continuation-v1/execution/supervisor-status-v1.json`. Only GPU7; original process creation/deadline/cleanup/accounting and in-worker audit unchanged. No original controller restart.
+5. After controller death, `PYTHON W/scripts/qd_ed_n25_cont_terminal.py --plan PLAN --status STATUS` independently checks the existing immutable result against old seal/new journal/receipts/source and recomputes counts, gates, native metadata and costs, without report.analyze or tensor reads. It writes separate root-terminal-review-v1.json and never replaces result. If and only if no result exists, explicit `--repair-missing-result` invokes the fallback writer; that is not an independent successful review, so run ordinary review afterward. The independent reviewer rejects duplicate attempt identifiers/counts before comparing terminal dictionaries and checks process cleanup for every newly dispatched attempt, including an invalid last attempt. A reserved-then-aborted undispatched attempt has explicit process absence, never an inferred PID. Missing process evidence for a dispatched attempt blocks root reconstruction. Metadata discrepancy rejects root reconstruction; no automatic experiment continuation follows.
+
+Complete logical40 promotion and whole-quad futility are unchanged; missing or disagreeing status yields INVALID while preserving the journal prefix/costs. Native activity/zero-gradient counts are descriptive, not new gates. Existing N25 validation79caa4 and N26 CPU predecessor gates remain inactive: a separate reviewed downstream evidence/source adapter is mandatory for any eventual logical-cohort outcome.
